  "prompt": "Should I get the Larkspur R7 or the Tamsin AX2 router from routers.md for a small flat where two people work from home?",
  "answer": "Get the Larkspur R7. It covers about 90 m², which is plenty for a small flat. It has four LAN ports and a built-in VPN server, which helps with working from home. It also costs 60 EUR less than the Tamsin AX2.\n\nThe Tamsin AX2 only makes sense if you want Wi-Fi 6E or a 2.5 gigabit port, and two remote workers probably don't need either."
